@startuml
!include style.iuml
mainframe class Proxy
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Proxy + Chain of Responsibility — as built (UML 2.5.1 class diagram)

class BoardController <<client>>
class ApiController <<client>>
interface AllocationService <<interface>> <<subject>> {
  +allocate(jobId : String, workerId : String, jobVersion : long) : Allocation
  +loadBoard(criteria : JobCriteria, selectedJobId : String) : BoardData
}
class AllocationServiceImpl <<real subject>>
class "$Proxy (java.lang.reflect.Proxy)" as JdkProxy <<proxy>>
class SecuredTransactionalProxy <<InvocationHandler>> {
  -target : Object
  -chain : List<Interceptor>
  +{static} wrap(iface : Class<T>, target : T, tx : TransactionRunner) : T
  +invoke(proxy : Object, method : Method, args : Object[]) : Object
}
interface Interceptor <<interface>> {
  +intercept(method : Method, next : Invocation) : Object
}
class SecurityInterceptor
class ExceptionTranslationInterceptor
class TransactionInterceptor
interface TransactionRunner <<interface>> <<port>> {
  +inTransaction(work : Supplier<R>) : R
}

BoardController --> AllocationService
ApiController --> AllocationService
AllocationService <|.. AllocationServiceImpl
AllocationService <|.. JdkProxy
JdkProxy --> "1" SecuredTransactionalProxy : handler
SecuredTransactionalProxy --> "1" AllocationServiceImpl : target
SecuredTransactionalProxy o--> "1..*" Interceptor : chain {ordered}
Interceptor <|.. SecurityInterceptor
Interceptor <|.. ExceptionTranslationInterceptor
Interceptor <|.. TransactionInterceptor
TransactionInterceptor --> "1" TransactionRunner

note right of SecurityInterceptor
  1. @RequiresRole check
  (protection proxy; before any database work)
end note
note right of ExceptionTranslationInterceptor
  2. OptimisticLock / DuplicateKey
  → ConcurrencyConflictException (409)
end note
note right of TransactionInterceptor
  3. @Transactional: begin, commit,
  roll back on any exception
end note
note bottom of SecuredTransactionalProxy
  Before: one invoke() did all three jobs and decoded SQLSTATE "23505".
  After: each concern is one Interceptor; a new one (timing, per-job authorisation)
  needs no change here (Open/Closed).
end note
@enduml
